# Files Prettier must never reformat.
#
# `docs/` holds *mirrored* documentation: verbatim copies of upstream sources
# (and machine-generated indexes/manifests/whats-new entries). Reformatting
# these files would corrupt the mirror — altering content that must remain
# byte-for-byte identical to its source — and would inject noise into every
# change-tracking diff, making code reviews harder. The entire directory is
# therefore excluded to guarantee the integrity of the mirroring pipeline.
# Only project-owned files at the repository root (README, NOTICE,
# configuration files) are kept formatted.
docs/

# Generated lockfile that is not meant to be hand-edited. uv.lock is produced
# by uv — the only package manager this project uses (there is no
# package.json, and Prettier itself runs via `npx -y`, which creates no
# lockfile) — and is committed only for reproducible installs. Reformatting
# it is pointless: the next `uv lock` or dependency upgrade overwrites any
# formatting changes, and the churn would only add noise to diffs that makes
# dependency audits harder. It is excluded to keep diffs clean and focused on
# actual code changes.
uv.lock

# Virtualenvs and caches: local-only directories that package managers and the
# Python runtime create for dependency isolation and bytecode caching. They
# contain no project source code, are never committed to version control (they
# belong in .gitignore, not the repository), and are large directory trees that
# Prettier should never waste time traversing.
.venv/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
